# SCINTX environment variables
# Copy to .env and adjust, or export before `make run` / `./bin/scintx`.
# The binary does not load .env automatically — use your shell, direnv, or:
#   set -a && source .env && set +a && make run

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTTP server
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Listen address for the gateway (host:port or :port).
# Default: :8080
SCINTX_ADDR=:8080

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inbound API authentication (clients → gateway)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profiles: off (default) | hmac | bearer | hmac,bearer
# When enabled, all routes except GET /v1/.well-known/scintx require auth.
# Well-known advertises the active auth_profiles.
#
# SCINTX_AUTH=off
# SCINTX_AUTH=hmac
# SCINTX_AUTH_HMAC_KEYS=demo:change-me-shared-secret
# SCINTX_AUTH=bearer
# SCINTX_AUTH_BEARER_TOKENS=change-me-token
# SCINTX_AUTH=hmac,bearer
# SCINTX_AUTH_MAX_SKEW=5m

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage (scintx.Store)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Backend: memory | sqlite | postgres
# Default / unset: memory — ephemeral forwarder (process + return; lost on restart).
# Set sqlite or postgres only when you want durable submissions/results/events.
# SCINTX_STORE=memory
# SCINTX_STORE=sqlite
# SCINTX_STORE=postgres

# SQLite file path (when SCINTX_STORE=sqlite). Parent dirs are created.
# Use :memory: for an ephemeral in-process DB.
# Default: data/scintx.db
SCINTX_SQLITE_PATH=./data/scintx.db

# Postgres connection URL (required when SCINTX_STORE=postgres).
# Example: postgres://scintx:scintx@localhost:5432/scintx?sslmode=disable
# SCINTX_DATABASE_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cache (provider result cache — api.CacheInfo)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Backend: none | ristretto | redis
#   ristretto — in-process (most common local Go cache; Dgraph TinyLFU)
#   redis     — shared across instances (github.com/redis/go-redis)
# Default: none
SCINTX_CACHE=none

# TTL for cached successful provider results (Go duration).
# Default: 1h
SCINTX_CACHE_TTL=1h

# Redis URL (required when SCINTX_CACHE=redis).
# Example: redis://localhost:6379/0
# SCINTX_REDIS_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Policy
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which PolicyEngine factory to load at process start.
# Registered today: yaml | example
# Default: yaml
SCINTX_POLICY_ENGINE=yaml

# Directory of YAML policy documents (*.yaml / *.yml).
# Used only when SCINTX_POLICY_ENGINE=yaml.
# Each file's metadata.id is a valid submission policy_ref.
# Default: policies  (relative to process working directory)
SCINTX_POLICIES_DIR=./policies

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workers / backpressure (optional pool; single binary by default)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How jobs are scheduled:
#   local — in-process worker pool (default; one binary is enough)
#   queue — shared jobs table with lease claims (multi-process auto-balance)
# Default: local
SCINTX_WORKER_MODE=local

# Max jobs admitted at once (local: running+queued; queue: see MAX_PENDING_JOBS).
# When full, Submit returns ErrBackpressure → HTTP 429 + Retry-After.
# Default: workers + max(64, 2*workers)
# Set to 0 for unlimited (local demos only).
SCINTX_MAX_INFLIGHT=72

# Concurrent Process() slots (must be ≤ MAX_INFLIGHT). Scale this up on bigger boxes.
# In queue mode this is claim concurrency per process.
# Default: min(8, max(4, 2*NumCPU)), clamped to MAX_INFLIGHT
SCINTX_WORKERS=8

# Optional: set waiting queue size instead of MAX_INFLIGHT (local mode).
# When set, max_inflight = WORKERS + JOB_QUEUE_SIZE (overrides MAX_INFLIGHT).
# SCINTX_JOB_QUEUE_SIZE=64

# --- Queue mode (SCINTX_WORKER_MODE=queue) ---
# Requires a shared store (sqlite or postgres). HTTP enqueues; any process claims.
# Dead workers: lease expires and another process reclaims the job.
# SCINTX_JOB_LEASE=2m
# SCINTX_JOB_POLL=200ms
# SCINTX_MAX_PENDING_JOBS=1000
# SCINTX_JOB_MAX_ATTEMPTS=8
# SCINTX_WORKER_ID=gateway-1

# Horizontal scale example:
#   SCINTX_STORE=postgres SCINTX_CACHE=redis SCINTX_WORKER_MODE=queue
#   run N gateway processes — work auto-balances via ClaimJob.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Webhooks (CloudEvent delivery)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Subscriber URL. When set, every stored CloudEvent is POSTed asynchronously.
# SCINTX_WEBHOOK_URL=https://registry.example/hooks/scintx

# HMAC-SHA256 shared secret (required when URL is set).
# Signature header: X-Scintx-Signature: t=<unix>,v1=<hex>
# Signed payload: "<unix>.<raw-body>"
# Also sends Content-Digest: sha-256=:base64: (RFC 9530).
# SCINTX_WEBHOOK_SECRET=change-me

# Per-attempt HTTP timeout (Go duration). Default: 10s
# SCINTX_WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT=10s

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adjudication forwarding (optional; off by default)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# After POST /v1/submissions/{id}/adjudicate, optionally fan out an *anonymous*
# signal (decision allow|deny + PURL only — no actor/rationale/submission id)
# to listed providers that advertise accepts_adjudications and implement
# AdjudicationReceiver.
# Empty / unset = disabled.
# Example:
# SCINTX_FORWARD_ADJUDICATIONS=osv,ossindex
# SCINTX_FORWARD_ADJUDICATIONS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Providers
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Comma-separated provider IDs to load. Empty = all registered factories.
# The default provider set is osv, ossindex, argus. malware-bazaar is
# tracked (SCINTX-110) but not built yet.
# Examples:
#   SCINTX_PROVIDERS=osv,ossindex              # vulnerability only (no malware)
#   SCINTX_PROVIDERS=osv,ossindex,argus        # full live set (default)
#   SCINTX_PROVIDERS=osv,ossindex              # omit argus if no ARGUS_API_KEY
# SCINTX_PROVIDERS=

# OSV.dev API base URL for the "osv" provider (no trailing slash).
# Default: https://api.osv.dev
# SCINTX_OSV_BASE_URL=https://api.osv.dev
# Optional outbound auth for private OSV mirrors / API gateways:
# SCINTX_OSV_BEARER_TOKEN=
# SCINTX_OSV_API_KEY=

# Sonatype OSS Index / Guide ("ossindex" provider).
# Auth is required. Prefer interactive local setup:
#   scintx auth ossindex
# That stores a Guide PAT in the OS keyring (or ~/.config/scintx/credentials).
# For CI, inject SCINTX_OSSINDEX_TOKEN from your secret store instead.
# Without credentials the provider is skipped at startup (so policy is not
# flooded with provider_4xx → review).
# Create a Guide PAT: https://guide.sonatype.com
# SCINTX_OSSINDEX_TOKEN=
# Optional username (Guide PAT ignores it; defaults to "scintx"):
# SCINTX_OSSINDEX_USER=
# Base URL (no trailing slash). Default: https://ossindex.sonatype.org
# (Guide Compatibility API: https://api.guide.sonatype.com)
# SCINTX_OSSINDEX_BASE_URL=https://ossindex.sonatype.org

# Argus ("argus" provider) — malware scan of VSIX artifact bytes
# (YARA + TLSH + multi-agent LLM, the OpenVSX pipeline). Argus scans
# artifact bytes, not PURLs; the gateway hydrates blob bytes onto
# Artifact.Content before Assess. Auth is required (scan scope).
# For CI, inject ARGUS_API_KEY from your secret store.
# Without credentials the provider fails per-scan (not skipped at startup).
# Create a key: https://app.yeethsecurity.com
# ARGUS_API_KEY=
# Base URL (no trailing slash). Default: https://api.yeethsecurity.com
# ARGUS_BASE_URL=https://api.yeethsecurity.com
# Total scan+poll ceiling (Go duration). Default: 120s
# ARGUS_SCAN_TIMEOUT=120s

# Optional config dir override (credentials file lives here):
# SCINTX_CONFIG_DIR=
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev / CI scripts only (not read by the scintx binary)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# When set to 1, ./scripts/check.sh also fails if go generate dirty's git.
# CI sets this; local make check usually leaves it unset.
# CHECK_GENERATED=1
